\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Give me the wings of faith to rise
\par Within the veil, and see
\par The saints above, how great their joys,
\par How bright their glories be.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Once they were mourners here below,
\par And poured out cries and tears;
\par They wrestled hard, as we do now,
\par With sins, and doubts, and fears.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I ask them whence their victory came;
\par They, with united breath,
\par Ascribe their conquest to the Lamb,
\par Their triumph to His death.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. They marked the footsteps that He trod,
\par His zeal inspired their breast;
\par And, following their incarnate God,
\par Possess the promise rest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Our glorious Leader claims our praise
\par For His own pattern given;
\par While the long cloud of witnesses
\par Show the same path to heaven.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

